# Vaelora — Art Performance and Memory Budget Framework v0.3

This document defines what to measure. Numerical hard limits are not invented before representative Stage-2 hardware measurements.

## 1. Why art performance is a design concern

Vaelora targets Android, Web and desktop with maps up to 80×50. The art pipeline must therefore control:

- texture memory;
- alpha overdraw;
- texture switches/draw calls;
- visible instance count;
- shader complexity;
- animation texture footprint;
- load time;
- package size.

## 2. Metrics recorded per family

- source PNG bytes;
- imported texture memory;
- atlas dimensions if packed;
- alpha occupied percentage;
- average/max transparent padding;
- number of variants;
- animation frames/facings;
- visible instance count in benchmark camera;
- draw calls/batches;
- frame time contribution;
- peak memory during largest-map scene;
- loading time.

## 3. Texture-memory estimation

Final 2× RGBA art is high quality but can be expensive when decoded. Review tools should estimate uncompressed RGBA memory as `width × height × 4`, with mipmap overhead shown separately when enabled.

This estimate is not a substitute for Godot’s importer/runtime measurement.

## 4. Variant discipline

Variants exist to defeat repetition, not to maximize content count.

Initial target counts are deliberately modest:

- open terrains: 4;
- forest/hills: 4;
- mountain: 3;
- peak: 2;
- coast base: 3 plus 18 reusable shoreline edges (3 morphology variants × 6 directions);
- shallow/open sea: 4 each.

Add a variant only when a repetition test demonstrates a visible problem that composition/material jitter cannot solve safely.

## 5. Animation cost

A six-facing, six-frame animation can multiply sprite footprint quickly. Before animating every role, calculate:

`frame size × 6 facings × frames × factions × actions`.

Animation is therefore reserved for high-value actions first.

## 6. Overdraw profile

Large transparent Sprite2D canvases can consume fill rate. Review report should flag:

- units/props with very low alpha occupancy;
- effect textures covering multiple tiles;
- stacked fog/territory/selection layers with full-screen transparency;
- city canvases dominated by empty space.

## 7. Performance profiles

Vaelora may expose presentation profiles without changing gameplay truth:

### Full

Accepted art, optional water highlight motion, normal feedback effects.

### Reduced motion

Static water/environmental motion and reduced non-essential effects.

### Constrained target

Same sprites and gameplay information, but optional cosmetic animation/effects disabled. Do not remove critical information or downgrade terrain identity.

## 8. Representative benchmark scenes

Measure at minimum:

1. 19-hex visual slice;
2. dense city/units view;
3. forest-heavy view;
4. coast/archipelago view;
5. largest 80×50 generated map at overview zoom;
6. worst-case UI + fog + territory + units visible.

## 9. Platform evidence

Record on representative Stage-2 devices/browsers:

- Android low-end floor candidate;
- Web browser/OS combinations;
- Windows baseline;
- macOS baseline;
- Linux baseline.

Hard art budgets are approved only after those measurements exist.
